RAWKEYS.CONF(5)

# NAME

rawkeys.conf - rawkeys global keyboard policy

# DESCRIPTION

rawkeys uses libconfig syntax. System configuration is read from
_/etc/rawkeys/rawkeys.conf_. User configuration overlays it from
_$XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME/rawkeys/rawkeys.conf_ or _~/.config/rawkeys/rawkeys.conf_.
Supplying *-c* selects one explicit file instead.

The top-level settings are *xkb*, *commands*, and *bindings*. Unknown settings
are rejected.

# XKB

The *xkb* group accepts:

*per\_window*
	Boolean. When true, preserve XKB core-keyboard group state per
	rawm-admitted focused client. The default is true.

# COMMANDS

*commands* is a group whose members are non-empty argv lists. No shell parsing
or interpolation is performed.

```
commands = {
  terminal = ("xterm");
  tag_name = ("rawmenu", "-M", "input", "-p", "tag");
};
```

# BINDINGS

*bindings* is a list of groups. Every binding requires *modifiers*, *key*, and
*target*. The same modifier/key pair may appear only once.

*modifiers*
	A list containing any of *Shift*, *Control*, *Mod1*, *Mod2*, *Mod3*,
	*Mod4*, or *Mod5*.

*key*
	An X keysym name accepted by Xlib.

*target = "exec"*
	Requires *command*, naming one entry in *commands*. No action or action
	arguments are accepted.

*target = "rawpanel"*
	Requires *action*. Version 0.1 accepts *toggle\_visibility*, *volume\_up*,
	*volume\_down*, and *volume\_mute*. The action must also be advertised by the
	currently running rawpanel authority.

*target = "rawm"*
	Requires *action*. The action must be advertised by the current rawm
	authority. Supported configuration arguments follow rawm protocol semantics:
	*number* for directional/index/delta operations, *tag* for tag selectors,
	*layout* for layout selection, *delta* or *factor* for master-factor
	changes, and *restart* for the quit command.

For *rename\_tag*, *capture* names a configured argv vector. rawkeys captures
one stdout line and forwards it as rawm's text payload. Other rawm actions do
not accept *capture*.

Example:

```
bindings = (
  { modifiers = ("Mod4"); key = "j";
    target = "rawm"; action = "focus_stack"; number = 1; },

  { modifiers = (); key = "XF86AudioMute";
    target = "rawpanel"; action = "volume_mute"; },

  { modifiers = ("Mod4"); key = "Return";
    target = "exec"; command = "terminal"; },

  { modifiers = ("Mod4"); key = "n";
    target = "rawm"; action = "rename_tag"; capture = "tag_name"; }
);
```

# AUTHORITY BOUNDARIES

rawkeys owns key grabs and XKB policy only. It does not implement rawm actions,
panel state, volume state, session supervision, pointer move/resize, or program
discovery.

# SEE ALSO

*rawkeys*(1), *rawm*(1), *rawpanel*(1)
